Fillets: a rounding rolling on both edges of a lens into the lens's ends,
where they meet and the rounding vanishes in a point (mitcad#343).

The case: a key on a shaft ends in a lens between the key's convex arc and
the shaft's concave arc; only the convex arc is rounded, with a radius
wider than the lens. The ball touches the key and rolls on the lens's
concave edge; where its contact on the key reaches the key's sides (the
edges between the key and the shaft) it rolls on those too, up to the
lens's ends, where the two edges meet and the rounding vanishes. The
walk's first step starts in the middle and ends at both sides; the walk
went on rolling on both edges at its last end, but then back from its
first end with the faces and edges of the steps at the other end, and
failed; where a side edge was split by a vertex short of the lens's end,
the walk stopped there (the edge's other face holds the end vertex), and
the corners failed.

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine: the walk back from the first
  step's start goes on with that step's faces, edges and obstacles (saved
  after it), its contacts there taken to be on their edges; a blend
  rolling on two edges, one of which ended at a vertex short of the
  spine's end vertex where another edge of its reference face, not
  tangent across, takes it on (as StartSol finds it), goes on rolling
  (RollsOnPastVertex) instead of ending at the face at the end.
- ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformSurf (rolling on two edges): the line's
  sections narrower than 5e-4 of the radius at an end where both contacts
  lie within a hundredth of the radius of the spine's end vertex are
  dropped (ChFi3d_EndRstRstBeforeVanishing): the approximation fails on
  sections of almost no width; the corner moves that end to the vertex
  (ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd), the blend ending in a point.

Upstream: new.
